# H-MAD per-run telemetry/state (runtime artifact, not skill source).
# `.h-mad/*` not `.h-mad/` — git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so the negation below would silently do nothing.
.h-mad/*
# The wire registry is the durable record of which connections were verified
# and against which base; 5f cannot return PASS while it is untracked.
!.h-mad/wires.jsonl

# H-MAD audit-completion markers. `hmad-dispatch.sh` writes `<report-path>.done`
# as the transport signal that a subagent finished writing; the coordinator polls
# the marker and then reads the REPORT, which is what gets committed. So a marker
# never carries information the tracked report does not already hold — measured
# 2026-09-14: all 88 in this tree had a tracked report and none was an orphan.
# They were standing untracked noise in `git status` across six consecutive
# handoffs, which is how a real untracked file gets lost in the list.
*.done

# Another lane's phase pointers, left behind by the gateway-consolidation and
# website-source-grounding runs. Nothing in THIS repo reads or writes them —
# `grep -rn lanestate` over every .py/.sh returns only handoff prose — and both
# lanes have since closed, so the contents are stale in both directions
# (`wsg.phase=4` with WSG Phase 5 closed; `gateway.phase=5` with #18 archived).
lanestate/
